#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:5
#: f1014bf92a9040debc1652296290a3d6
msgid "Multiwii Serial Protocol (MSP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:7
#: 35e3ad85e2584dcc9c51d99d1e8ee678
msgid "ArduPilot supports the MSP protocol for telemetry, OSDs, and sensors via any of its serial ports. This allows ArduPilot to send its telemetry data to MSP compatible devices, such as DJI goggles, for On Screen Display (OSD) (See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2`). It can also be used by external OSDS, such as MWOSD, when setup for MSP protocol (ie betaflight/Inav)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:10
#: abec5aa92956421180fbcdad58ed732e
msgid "Protocol overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:12
#: 94c7a67c65f54f6bbd5a9767b9445955
msgid "MSP is the main communication protocol used by all Betaflight derived flight stacks. It's a binary message based protocol used for control, telemetry and sensors. ArduPilot's MSP protocol module is ported from Betaflight and iNav, and supports both MSPV1 and MSPV2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:16
#: 024e77b7f83e45fa904fcfee3a598ed0
msgid "At the moment, the ArduPilot implementation supports:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:18
#: 3f12d7d4873b4d8898468fd1729ad0d8
msgid "MSP Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:19
#: ca67618d61144a47a86e7957508026ac
msgid "MSP Telemetry OSDs such as DJI FPV Goggles, FatShark's ByteFrost and SharkByte, MWOSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:20
#: 55ded9cce0dc48379279c7041176d36d
msgid "MSP DisplayPort OSDs such as FatShark's Shark Byte and MWOSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:21
#: 5b87d6438b374ef086176de1cf0ee510
msgid "MSP Sensors such as lidar, optical flow, gps, barometer, magnetometer and airspeed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:23
#: c164cd45ec9e4f24938b6534f854f821
msgid "ArduPilot configuration via MSP protocol is not supported, so for instance the Betaflight configurator won't work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:27
#: 5abbbbdb554b48a4a2b69d95976aac13
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:29
#: 9333567f1ec54d5bb54befd73b2f4467
msgid "MSP requires a free serial port, and its speed defaults to 115200 baud. Below SERIAL2 is used for the examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:31
#: 22eba0b6b3204eee88dc4b44e0900ced
msgid "There are 3 MSP backends selected by serial protocol:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:33
#: f2172bb87c2d43d99f1c16eca7d93629
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 33 is for DJI FPV or RE Goggles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:34
#: 95e07f5acbee4bbc8c3629c3a2e83795
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 32 is for sensors or generic MSP telemetry usage and MWOSD configured for MSP telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:35
#: 327e3dc15cd64e04a5cc68267ee6dfef
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 42 is for DisplayPort OSDs (aka CANVAS MODE) such as FatShark's SharkByte"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:37
#: 3f92ef077e074271bcd1fea1f0f4f349
msgid "There are 2 different protocols to try to maintain compatibility with DJI's evolving hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:39
#: 487fe9177f0240489d1e2e55878138d0
msgid "When :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 33 is selected the protocol decoder can work in polling mode (default) or in \"telemetry push\" mode. When working in polling mode, both TX and RX must be connected to the MSP telemetry transceiver. While in push mode only the TX line is used. To enable push mode, simply set :ref:`MSP_OPTIONS<MSP_OPTIONS>` bit 0 to \"1\"; to disable set it to \"0\" (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview-4.2.rst:41
#: fd853ac0ecfd4f1a9f87439f1fa1814c
msgid "MSP sensors such as the Matek 3901-L0X are supported by both protocols."
msgstr ""
